  "lineage": "Malian Wassoulou region (south of Bamako, between the Niger and Sankarani rivers, populated by the Wassoulou Fula and Bambara peoples) popular-music tradition extending the older donso ngoni (hunters harp-lute) hunters-music tradition into modern band format; built on the kamele ngoni (the Wassoulou youth harp-lute, a smaller more melodic adaptation of the donso ngoni), female-vocal foregrounded — codified through Oumou Sangaré (the Wassoulou voice from her 1989 Moussolou breakthrough onward), Sali Sidibé, Coumba Sidibé, Nahawa Doumbia",
